    narr:narration """A recorded conversation on cutover sequencing for a four-site platform migration. [Tanya opens by framing the settled cutover shape and asking for a rota-side read before it hardens](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_2), stating the [one-site-at-a-time rule: soak clean before the next starts, never two cutovers at once](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_7). [Freya accepts and asks for the shape](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_5), then grounds the constraint in [supervisor arithmetic — four pulled per cutover night against eleven across the region](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_11), sharpening it as [not hard but impossible: the people don't exist](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_12) and [recasting last week's risk argument as arithmetic](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_14). [Xavier ranks it the strongest case yet, ahead of the data-drift and unbounded-risk arguments](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_15), and [Freya calls it the one that doesn't move](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_16). [Tanya commits to leading with it at the steering group](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_17). A second benefit surfaces in [supervisors carrying learning from the first cutover into the second](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_18), which [Xavier generalizes as one learning curve rather than four teams erring in parallel](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_19). [Xavier also notes the replica and reference-data rules silently assume a single open cutover window](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_25), and [Tanya closes the parallel option outright](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_26). The exchange ends with [Freya asking for early dates and a commitment that soaks never get shortened](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_28), which [Tanya holds](narr:Expr_2HalyardOpsReadiness20260915_29).""" ;
